{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 21:20:33 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 04:20:33 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nThe two original P1s are addressed in the tree. WebSocket endpoint acceptance no longer looks up a served path or sends an admission frame ([ws.cljc:467](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:467), [ws.cljc:545](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:545)). The client opens on its socket’s open event ([ws.cljc:266](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:266)). RPC mint failures now distinguish retryable results from terminal ones and route terminal results through the shared loss translation ([rpc.cljc:425](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc:425), [rpc.cljc:443](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc:443), [rpc.cljc:513](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc:513)).\n\n**New P1 — early inbound frames can be lost or delivered out of order.** The client can write as soon as its socket opens, while the server handle is still pending; `deliver!` queues those frames ([ws.cljc:284](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:284)). `accept-slot!` reads that queue, then separately changes the phase to `:open` and clears it ([ws.cljc:545](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:545)). A frame queued between those operations is erased. A frame arriving after the phase change can also be deposited ahead of the older queued frames being replayed. The endpoint test exercises inbound delivery only *after* acknowledgement ([ws_test.cljc:283](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/ws_test.cljc:283)). Make the queue handoff atomic with the phase change and preserve frame order; cover the before-acknowledgement case.\n\nI did not edit files or rerun suites. The supplied JVM, Node, and Dart results establish suite health, but do not exercise this race. Slice-7 and slice-8 are outside this verdict.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
